---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SiteNav from "../components/SiteNav.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Regex Cheat Sheet"
  description="Privacy Policy for Regex Cheat Sheet. Learn how we handle your data, analytics, and privacy in compliance with GDPR and CCPA."
>
  <SiteNav />

  <main id="main-content" class="container-wide main-prose">
    <div class="prose-wrapper">
      <h1 class="page-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="last-updated">Last Updated: August 29, 2026</p>

      <div class="content-block">
        <p>
          At <strong>regexsheet</strong> (regexsheet.com), accessible from
          https://regexsheet.com, one of our main priorities is the privacy of
          our visitors. This Privacy Policy document outlines the types of
          information that is collected and recorded by regexsheet and
          how we use it.
        </p>
        <p>
          This policy applies globally, including for users under the General
          Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) in the European Union and the
          California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA).
        </p>

        <h2>1. The Live Regex Tester</h2>
        <p>
          The interactive Regex Tester tool provided on this website runs <strong
            >entirely locally in your web browser</strong
          >. We do not send, transmit, collect, or store any of the regular
          expressions or text strings you test to our servers. Your data remains
          strictly on your own device.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Information We Collect (Analytics)</h2>
        <p>
          To understand how visitors use our site and to improve the user
          experience, we may use standard analytics tools (such as Google
          Analytics and Google Tag Manager). These tools collect aggregated, non-personally
          identifiable information, which may include:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Browser type and version</li>
          <li>Operating system</li>
          <li>Pages visited and time spent on pages</li>
          <li>Referring websites or search terms</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This data is used strictly for analytical purposes to improve the
          content and performance of the website.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Cookies and Web Beacons</h2>
        <p>
          Like any other website, regexsheet uses "cookies". These
          cookies are used to store information including visitors' preferences,
          such as the dark/light mode theme toggle.
        </p>
        <p>
          If analytics services (like Google Analytics) are active, they may set
          their own cookies to track site usage. You can choose to disable
          cookies through your individual browser options. Disabling cookies
          will not prevent you from using the core features of this cheat sheet.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Third-Party Links and Services</h2>
        <p>
          Our website contains links to other websites, such as GitHub for
          open-source contributions or third-party platforms for donations
          (e.g., GitHub Sponsors). We have no control over and assume no
          responsibility for the content, privacy policies, or practices of any
          third-party sites or services.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Your Privacy Rights (GDPR & CCPA)</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on your location, you may have the right to request access
          to the data we collect, request correction or deletion of that data,
          or object to its processing. Because we do not collect personally
          identifiable information (PII) or require user accounts, there is no
          personal data tied to your identity on our servers to delete.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Consent</h2>
        <p>
          By using our website, you hereby consent to our Privacy Policy and
          agree to its Terms.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          If you have additional questions or require more information about our
          Privacy Policy, you can reach out via our public GitHub repository
          issues page.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>

<style>
  .main-prose {
    padding-top: var(--space-xl);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-xxl);
  }

  .prose-wrapper {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
    padding: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .page-title {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-xs) 0;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .last-updated {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-xl) 0;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-md);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .content-block {
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .content-block h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: var(--space-xl) 0 var(--space-sm) 0;
  }

  .content-block p {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md) 0;
  }

  .content-block ul {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md) 0;
    padding-left: var(--space-xl);
    list-style-type: disc;
  }

  .content-block li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .content-block strong {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .prose-wrapper {
      padding: var(--space-md);
      border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    }
  }
</style>
